  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SALAR Local self-government in Armenia 2022-2026 - Local self-government in ARM</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SALAR Lokalt sj&#xe4;lvstyre i Armenien 2022-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sveriges kommuner och regioner (SKR) har till Sida ans&#xf6;kt om finansiellt st&#xf6;d, uppg&#xe5;ende till 16,7 milj. sv. kr., f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra ett projekt, ben&#xe4;mnt &#xab;Support to Decentralisation and Local Self-Government Reform in Armenia&#xbb;, under perioden juli 2022 - december 2023 (etapp 1). Syftet med projektet &#xe4;r att praktiskt kapacitetsst&#xe4;rka det armeniska kommunf&#xf6;rbundet, och att genomf&#xf6;ra insatser i ett antal pilotkommuner, baserade p&#xe5; en svensk modell f&#xf6;r utveckling av lokalt sj&#xe4;lvstyre, och utveckla en l&#xe5;ngsiktig &#xab;roadmap&#xbb; f&#xf6;r utveckling av relationer p&#xe5; demokratisk grund mellan kommunledning och lokalbefolkning, samt utveckling av en kommunal infrastruktur av tillhandah&#xe5;llna tj&#xe4;nster</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Swedish Association of Local Authorities and Regions (SALAR) has applied to Sida for financial support, amounting to SEK 16.7 million. Swed. Cr., to implement a project, entitled &#xab;Support to decentralization and Local Self-Government Reform in Armenia&#xbb;, during the period July 2022 - December 2023 (stage 1). The aim of the project is to practically capacity-enhance the Union of Municipalities of Armenia, and to carry out actions in a number of pilot municipalities, based on a Swedish model for the development of local self-government, and develop a long-term &#xab;roadmap&#xbb; for the development of relations on a democratic basis between municipal management and the local population, as well as the development of a municipal infrastructure of services provided</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to enhance commitment, capacity, and trust among national and local stakeholders for decentralisation and local self-government reforms in Armenia. It will aim to foster a multi-level policy dialogue as a cross-cutting pathway of change, informed by evidence on institutional conditions and capacities at the local level, and underscored by concrete experiences of improving local self-governance practices.

SALAR focuses its interventions on fiscal decentralisation, decentralisation in the field of education and contributes to objectives linked with wider awareness raising, advocacy and strengthening of strategic reform leadership.

Outcome 1. Institutional framework for decentralisation: actors across levels have aligned in their understanding of the decentralisation and LSG reforms and are prepared for implementation

Outcome 2. Fiscal decentralisation: through collaboration of all actors, fiscal decentralisation is operationalised for the Armenian context. Capacity, tools and processes to implement fiscal decentralisation co-developed by critical actors.

Outcome 3. Sector decentralisation (from 2024 onward): sector ministry (Ministry of Education, Science, Culture and Sports) and LSGs have strengthened capacity and capabilities for management and delivery of delegated decentralised service functions .</narrative>
  </description>
